    <statement><p>Convert from polar to rectangular coordinates:</p>
<p><m>\mathbf{(a)}\quad(4,\frac{\pi}{6})\quad\Rightarrow_{(x,y)}\quad</m>(<fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0001"/>,<fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0002"/>)</p>
<p><m>\mathbf{(b)}\quad(9,\pi)\quad\Rightarrow_{(x,y)}\quad</m>(<fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0003"/>,<fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0004"/>)</p>
<p><m>\mathbf{(c)}\quad(8,\frac{\pi}{3})\quad\Rightarrow_{(x,y)}\quad</m>(<fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0005"/>,<fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0006"/>)</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3.4641</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-9</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6.9282</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\mathbf{(a)}</m> Since <m>r=4</m> and <m>\theta =\frac{\pi}{6}</m>, we have:
<me>x=r\cos\theta=4\cos \frac{\pi}{6}=4\cdot \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}=3.4641</me>
<me>y=r\sin\theta=4\sin \frac{\pi}{6}=4\cdot \frac12=2</me>
<me>\Downarrow</me>
<me>(x,y)=(3.4641,2)</me>



<m>\mathbf{(b)}</m> For <m>(9,\pi)</m> we have <m>r=9</m> and <m>\theta=\pi</m>. Hence,
<me>x=r\cos\theta=9\cos \pi=9\cdot -1=-9</me>
<me>y=r\sin\theta=9\sin \pi=9\cdot 0=0</me>
<me>\Downarrow</me>
<me>(x,y)=(-9,0)</me>



<m>\mathbf{(c)}</m> Since <m>r=8</m> and <m>\theta =\frac{\pi}{3}</m>, we have:
<me>x=r\cos\theta=8\cos \frac{\pi}{3}=8\cdot \frac12=4</me>
<me>y=r\sin\theta=8\sin \frac{\pi}{3}=8\cdot \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}=6.9282</me>
<me>\Downarrow</me>
<me>(x,y)=(4,6.9282)</me>


</solution>
